27:29.400 --> 27:31.560
What a shame!

27:33.690 --> 27:35.020
Dead?

27:35.020 --> 27:38.190
I'm... dead?

27:40.100 --> 27:42.020
Really?

27:42.020 --> 27:45.230
I went out like that?

27:45.230 --> 27:46.940
Gone at twenty?

27:47.480 --> 27:54.190
Why was I born, then?

27:54.190 --> 28:01.190
Did you just make us all on a whim?

28:04.440 --> 28:06.440
How the hell would I know why, huh?

28:08.730 --> 28:11.100
Yeah, so I made you on a whim!

28:12.770 --> 28:17.020
I made all you dipshits for my sheer enjoyment!

28:17.350 --> 28:19.520
What's wrong with that?

28:22.520 --> 28:25.270
Oops, I have to go.

28:25.600 --> 28:26.940
Got a date.

28:27.600 --> 28:28.440
A date?

28:28.810 --> 28:31.150
Yep. Time to wrap things up.

28:31.150 --> 28:34.810
Go straight that way and keep walking.

28:34.810 --> 28:36.730
You'll disappear in a jiffy.

28:37.310 --> 28:38.940
And my next life?

28:39.480 --> 28:40.600
Huh?

28:40.600 --> 28:41.440
My next life!

28:41.440 --> 28:47.440
Your what? I told you, it's over. Start walking!

28:47.810 --> 28:50.060
And disappear?

28:50.060 --> 28:51.440
No afterlife?

28:51.440 --> 28:55.770
We're done?

28:57.060 --> 28:59.940
It's really over?!

29:02.100 --> 29:05.440
For real, God? For real?

29:09.690 --> 29:15.150
Will you shut up? You saw how you got here.
You got a multi-angle shot of your brain exploding.

29:15.600 --> 29:20.650
A shocking documentary of your death, deftly edited by Moi!

29:21.350 --> 29:23.560
You are...

29:24.100 --> 29:26.560
DEAD!

29:28.060 --> 29:30.020
I'm...

29:31.690 --> 29:34.060
officially dead?

29:34.600 --> 29:36.560
I'm so sorry, Nishi!

29:57.650 --> 30:00.230
Straight ahead and disappear.

30:02.480 --> 30:07.190
So if I go that way... If I go the <i>other</i> way...

30:12.980 --> 30:17.020
Hey! What are you doing?! I'm gonna be late!

30:13.650 --> 30:17.020
Please, God, I'll do it right this time!

30:17.020 --> 30:18.850
Wait!

30:18.850 --> 30:21.810
Let me through! I'm going back!

30:23.020 --> 30:25.020
You just don't know when to give up, huh?

30:25.940 --> 30:27.810
You're gonna fade away.

30:27.810 --> 30:29.810
That's just how it works.

30:29.810 --> 30:32.270
See? You're already fading.

30:37.190 --> 30:40.270
I don't believe you! I'm not gonna disappear!

30:40.270 --> 30:41.270
I'm going back!

30:41.270 --> 30:42.600
Won't happen!

30:42.600 --> 30:46.730
I'm definitely, definitely, definitely, definitely going back!

30:49.270 --> 30:54.270
Not bad, but can you keep it up? With that body? That brain?

30:54.600 --> 30:55.850
I'm going back!

30:55.850 --> 30:58.270
I'm gonna take care of that creep!

30:58.270 --> 31:02.100
I'm gonna be stronger! More determined! Free and happy!

31:02.100 --> 31:05.770
Live life to the fullest!

31:09.270 --> 31:10.190
Pretty good!

31:13.480 --> 31:16.480
All right, give it your best shot!

31:16.480 --> 31:20.560
Yes! I'm going back! I'm gonna do this!

31:21.310 --> 31:23.980
I'm on your side! I'm on your side.

31:26.440 --> 31:29.480
It's your turn next, amigo.

31:29.480 --> 31:30.850
C'mon, get up!

31:30.850 --> 31:32.980
Get it up down there, too!

31:35.480 --> 31:40.230
N-Never! Never!

31:43.100 --> 31:44.770
Never again!

31:48.560 --> 31:49.770
Don't move!

31:56.980 --> 31:58.350
Yang, come here.

32:01.850 --> 32:05.310
Move and I'll blow your head off.

32:05.980 --> 32:08.310
I'm done being the loser.

32:09.650 --> 32:10.600
Give me the car keys!

32:11.940 --> 32:13.690
Nishi!

32:16.600 --> 32:18.350
You're on your own, sir!

32:18.730 --> 32:19.850
Come on, let's roll!

32:19.850 --> 32:20.850
No way!

32:20.850 --> 32:22.020
Get in!

32:24.560 --> 32:26.480
Wait!

32:29.480 --> 32:31.350
Atsu got wasted.

32:32.650 --> 32:34.690
It was my fault.

32:34.690 --> 32:38.730
They're in my car, so they won't get away.

32:40.190 --> 32:41.480
My apologies.

32:52.940 --> 32:55.350
This is crazy! We're gonna hit someone!

32:55.650 --> 32:57.850
Help!

33:04.850 --> 33:08.190
And a hero is born.

33:08.190 --> 33:09.850
Hands on the wheel!

33:10.480 --> 33:14.600
Don't worry, I'm on it! I'll protect you!

33:14.600 --> 33:16.350
I love you both.

33:16.600 --> 33:18.600
Eyes on the road, dumbass!

33:18.600 --> 33:23.770
Why are we running? Shouldn't we go to the police? It was self-defense, right?

33:23.770 --> 33:25.100
No! No! No!

33:25.100 --> 33:29.810
No cops, no questions, no regrets!

33:29.810 --> 33:31.060
I'm through with that!

33:31.060 --> 33:34.650
I'm making a break for it with you two!

33:34.650 --> 33:36.230
I'm gonna do what I want!

33:36.230 --> 33:37.600
No one's gonna get in my way!

33:37.600 --> 33:41.100
I'm following my heart's desires!

33:41.100 --> 33:43.230
Like an outlaw!

34:00.100 --> 34:02.730
<i>Hello there. Can you hear me?</i>

34:03.440 --> 34:10.350
<i>This is a bit sudden, but do you realize you were living in paradise till today?</i>

34:11.060 --> 34:18.310
<i>Like angels flying around in heaven.</i>

34:18.310 --> 34:23.020
<i>But now you're on an express train to the depths of hell!</i>

34:27.400 --> 34:31.810
You know the guy you smoked? That bald son of a bitch?

34:32.770 --> 34:35.310
His name was Atsu.

34:35.310 --> 34:43.690
A fine soccer player and athlete,
known as the Maradona of Osaka.

34:44.520 --> 34:49.600
For good and bad reasons both.

34:49.600 --> 34:55.650
He had a chiseled body like a wild animal!

34:55.650 --> 34:58.400
Not that it has to do with anything.

34:58.690 --> 35:04.770
So it seems you knew that he swings a piece around when he's collecting.

35:04.770 --> 35:11.230
You knew the car's filled with money and drugs too.

35:11.230 --> 35:15.100
This is a clear-cut armed robbery and murder case, if you ask me.

35:15.730 --> 35:23.060
A tragic murder, at that. The victim was abandoned by his parents at a young age, never knowing love.

35:23.560 --> 35:28.810
He'd been looking forward to seeing the World Cup with his girl.

35:28.810 --> 35:32.230
A model Japanese soccer fan.

35:32.850 --> 35:40.230
But just before the big game, he was killed by a young punk.

35:41.900 --> 35:46.980
Ah, the ever-egocentric, unfeeling youth of today!

35:46.980 --> 35:50.230
<i>Immature adults on the loose,</i>

35:50.230 --> 35:53.600
<i>everything a blur except their friends.</i>

35:53.600 --> 36:00.600
<i>Living life like a video game,
finger on the reset button! No empathy!</i>

36:01.810 --> 36:05.850
<i>You're on a roller coaster with no brakes!</i>

36:08.020 --> 36:11.150
It's not true! That's not what happened at all!

36:11.440 --> 36:18.810
Natural. Dramatic. A perfect synopsis for our sports-loving cops.

36:20.270 --> 36:23.690
What I'm sayin' is, the whole world's against you.

36:24.230 --> 36:25.900
This is it, kids!

36:26.900 --> 36:28.940
Make it a good game!

36:32.810 --> 36:35.350
Nice speech, old man.

36:35.350 --> 36:37.230
Will you stop it?!

36:38.230 --> 36:43.900
I can just imagine you sweating in front of a teleprompter!

36:41.810 --> 36:43.230
Nishi!

36:44.770 --> 36:45.900
It's improv!

36:47.400 --> 36:48.770
Okay.

36:49.060 --> 36:50.810
What exactly do you think is okay?

36:55.520 --> 37:02.560
This roller coaster you're trying to stop isn't something you'd
find in some Hollywood theme park—it's a genuine Angel Express!

37:03.980 --> 37:08.310
And I can see you moved to tears as you watch that mystic angel

37:08.310 --> 37:12.810
spread its wings and disappear into the sky!

37:13.270 --> 37:13.940
<i>Okay?</i>

37:13.940 --> 37:15.020
The fuck?!

37:39.060 --> 37:39.940
Shit!

37:50.980 --> 37:52.850
Nishi!

37:52.850 --> 37:54.480
Offside!

37:59.310 --> 38:02.310
Idiots, this ain't soccer!

38:05.520 --> 38:07.520
Now get in as close as you can!

38:08.770 --> 38:11.190
Offside trap!

39:12.980 --> 39:14.690
Stunt driving!

39:22.190 --> 39:23.730
My nose is bleeding!

39:23.730 --> 39:24.690
Mine too!

39:24.690 --> 39:26.690
Mine too!

39:27.650 --> 39:29.190
The bridge!

39:38.520 --> 39:41.560
What the fuck are you doing?!

40:03.480 --> 40:07.230
My Pitch, my little Pitch!

40:08.850 --> 40:10.270
Pitch!

40:10.270 --> 40:11.690
You came back! Pitch...

40:28.150 --> 40:30.150
No more fooling around.

40:30.770 --> 40:32.650
<i>We'll get 'em on the bridge.</i>

40:33.310 --> 40:38.730
<i>We're setting up the perfect defense.
Even Zidane and Figo couldn't get through.</i>

40:39.480 --> 40:40.730
<i>We'll get 'em.</i>

41:29.600 --> 41:31.190
A whale?

41:44.850 --> 41:46.770
What, you again?

41:46.770 --> 41:48.810
Not just yet!

41:50.730 --> 41:52.440
You there, Nishi?

41:53.270 --> 41:55.810
Are we... dead?

41:55.810 --> 41:57.060
You both there?

41:58.310 --> 41:59.310
Wait a sec.

42:00.980 --> 42:01.940
Where is it?

42:04.810 --> 42:05.650
Bingo!

42:09.440 --> 42:10.770
We're alive.

42:11.560 --> 42:12.560
Thank God!

42:12.560 --> 42:14.900
Seawater? Can't see shit.

42:16.440 --> 42:17.770
Near the harbor, maybe.

42:17.770 --> 42:20.020
Smells fishy.

42:25.900 --> 42:27.150
Have no fear!

42:27.150 --> 42:32.100
Fear takes the shape we're willing to give it!

42:32.100 --> 42:35.560
Let's light a candle in our hearts. Make it gleam.

42:35.560 --> 42:37.850
Try to enjoy the moment!

42:37.850 --> 42:40.940
Try thinking "this is fun," even if it's a lie!

42:43.270 --> 42:46.480
It'll shed a new light on things!

42:50.060 --> 42:53.230
Think back to our days in grade school.

42:53.230 --> 42:55.310
When we just played until the sun set,

42:55.310 --> 42:58.440
no restrictions or tomorrows.

42:59.060 --> 43:02.480
We didn't end up here 'cause we were chased!

43:02.480 --> 43:03.900
We came here seeking adventure!

43:04.230 --> 43:06.060
An epic journey!

43:06.560 --> 43:07.980
Let the adventure begin!

43:12.480 --> 43:14.980
Hey, there's a boat.

43:18.270 --> 43:19.730
Let's check it out!

43:20.560 --> 43:24.520
Lane Number 1, Nishi! Third Grade!

43:24.520 --> 43:25.440
And we're off!

43:29.690 --> 43:31.400
Let's go.

43:30.100 --> 43:31.400
Are you serious?

43:34.190 --> 43:37.600
Lane No. 2, Myon! Also 3rd Grade.

43:37.600 --> 43:38.730
Here I go!

43:55.980 --> 43:58.190
Wow, what a wreck.

43:58.650 --> 43:59.980
Can we climb up?

44:28.020 --> 44:29.770
Where are we?

44:29.770 --> 44:31.520
Wherever it is, it stinks.

44:31.520 --> 44:34.690
I'm starving!

44:34.690 --> 44:36.560
Good for my figure, though.

44:36.560 --> 44:39.440
Huh? Your body is <i>dope</i>!

44:39.440 --> 44:41.230
It's not like you've seen it.

44:41.230 --> 44:42.730
I just look slim.

44:43.650 --> 44:44.940
Show me, then!

44:44.940 --> 44:46.400
No way.

44:46.400 --> 44:47.770
Please!

44:47.770 --> 44:48.730
Nope!

44:48.730 --> 44:49.900
Please!

44:50.850 --> 44:52.190
Sugar on top!

44:52.190 --> 44:53.020
Nah!

44:53.020 --> 44:55.350
Aw, c'mon!

44:54.150 --> 44:55.350
Nishi!

44:55.350 --> 44:57.520
What now, huh?!

44:57.520 --> 44:59.690
You almost got us killed!

44:59.690 --> 45:03.270
Sure he was scum, but you just killed a guy!

45:03.270 --> 45:04.980
What's with the "enthusiasm"?

45:06.980 --> 45:08.730
I was killed.

45:08.730 --> 45:11.060
Shot by that creep.

45:11.060 --> 45:13.270
What the hell are you talking about?

45:13.270 --> 45:14.980
He's the one that's gone, dodo!

45:14.980 --> 45:20.190
Before that. See, I was so scared that I missed the timing to get angry.

45:20.190 --> 45:23.150
And that's when that baldy shot me.

45:24.230 --> 45:26.440
Then I was sucked up to heaven and...

45:26.980 --> 45:28.600
You've lost it.

45:28.600 --> 45:31.560
But I believed in myself, believed like nothing else,

45:31.560 --> 45:33.400
and I was back!

45:33.400 --> 45:37.770
To live true to yourself, sincerely, without restraint!

45:37.770 --> 45:42.060
I realized it's the only weapon against any wall!

45:44.980 --> 45:46.900
Okay, you've lost me.

45:46.900 --> 45:49.100
But <i>this</i> is where it got us!

45:49.100 --> 45:52.400
And we're only <i>here</i> because we were lucky!

45:52.400 --> 45:54.060
It's a miracle we're even alive.

45:54.770 --> 45:57.230
If this keeps up, we'll be dead in no time.

45:57.230 --> 45:58.440
Ahh! Who... who...

46:03.600 --> 46:09.480
I... I...

46:09.480 --> 46:11.560
I...

46:11.560 --> 46:17.520
I've got... a radio!

46:18.520 --> 46:19.400
What?

46:20.060 --> 46:21.230
A radio?

46:21.230 --> 46:24.270
This place is dangerous. We need to move!

46:24.270 --> 46:25.730
Hurry! Hurry!

46:26.520 --> 46:28.480
What?!

46:26.900 --> 46:30.770
C'mon, hurry! You've got to hurry!

46:28.480 --> 46:31.770
Hey! H-Hold on!

46:36.520 --> 46:37.730
Wh-What is this?

46:37.730 --> 46:39.060
An earthquake? A tsunami?

46:39.060 --> 46:41.940
You guys are reckless!

46:41.940 --> 46:43.310
The hell, old man?!

46:43.310 --> 46:44.980
Hurry up!

46:44.980 --> 46:48.520
Grab an oar and row!

46:46.650 --> 46:48.520
Nishi, get rowing!

46:50.730 --> 46:51.480
Tidal wave?

46:51.480 --> 46:52.520
Tsunami!

46:55.020 --> 46:58.690
Move it, people! Move!

47:01.100 --> 47:01.980
Over there!

47:02.900 --> 47:03.900
Almost there!

47:04.400 --> 47:05.980
Hang on!

47:25.980 --> 47:28.520
Meal time's over.

47:28.520 --> 47:30.230
We're okay now.

47:31.560 --> 47:32.980
Let's go up.

47:52.520 --> 47:56.600
Wow! It's like a secret base!

47:58.100 --> 48:01.230
TV, microwave, audio set, PC...

48:01.230 --> 48:02.480
You've got everything!

48:03.400 --> 48:04.810
You scavenged all this stuff?

48:06.850 --> 48:07.850
Ah, and food!

48:10.440 --> 48:14.190
It's all sexy lingerie! You dirty old man!

48:15.900 --> 48:17.940
It's even in the microwave.

48:19.230 --> 48:22.020
No power, huh?

48:22.020 --> 48:23.600
This stuff's just for show, then?

48:23.600 --> 48:25.150
Gross.

48:25.150 --> 48:26.810
Isn't it modern art?

48:28.730 --> 48:30.940
Want to freshen up?

48:31.520 --> 48:35.730
Clean yourself up with clean hot water?

48:35.730 --> 48:38.730
You mean have a bath?

48:36.270 --> 48:38.730
Yes! Yes!

48:39.560 --> 48:41.020
I'd like that!

48:41.020 --> 48:43.600
Yeah? Me too!

48:57.730 --> 48:59.310
This is bliss.

49:01.850 --> 49:04.770
But boy, we're in some mess.

49:04.770 --> 49:06.350
It's surreal.

49:07.400 --> 49:12.350
I mean, we're in God-knows-where enjoying a total stranger's hospitality.

49:12.350 --> 49:15.810
Having a bath! Unbelievable.

49:18.020 --> 49:22.310
Well, he's one nugget short of a happy meal, but he seems nice!

49:54.810 --> 49:58.600
No matter how old you get, a perv's a perv, huh?

49:59.100 --> 50:03.100
I feel like it's the first time we're having a real talk.

50:07.230 --> 50:10.230
We'll leave clean clothes here!

50:11.060 --> 50:14.270
Those bastards! Not very subtle, are they?

50:14.270 --> 50:17.520
We could pretend we're cosplaying... or maybe not.

50:17.520 --> 50:20.230
Hey, find something we can actually wear!

50:21.770 --> 50:23.980
Wow! Looks amazing!

50:25.100 --> 50:26.690
You made this?

50:27.190 --> 50:28.480
You made this, gramps?

50:28.900 --> 50:30.650
Should've seen him at work!

50:30.650 --> 50:34.900
Really? It's like a New York sushi bar!

50:34.900 --> 50:37.900
Where'd you learn to cook, gramps?

50:43.940 --> 50:45.480
Whoa!

50:48.730 --> 50:50.270
Yeah, it's delicious!

50:50.270 --> 50:51.900
Five stars in my book!

50:52.270 --> 50:54.650
Bon appétit!

50:56.480 --> 50:58.060
Wow.

50:58.060 --> 50:59.440
What a meal!

50:59.440 --> 51:00.940
Thanks!

51:00.940 --> 51:04.850
Much better than some fancy conveyor-belt sushi bar in Kita.

51:05.770 --> 51:10.730
Conveyor-belt sushi. They started making places that look like they're straight out of America last year.

51:10.730 --> 51:12.270
Conveyor-belt sushi.

51:13.310 --> 51:16.190
Rotating sushi.

51:18.690 --> 51:20.690
Not like that!

51:21.980 --> 51:23.150
No, no.

51:23.150 --> 51:25.560
In front of the customers.

51:31.400 --> 51:33.980
Mine's dead too.

51:34.730 --> 51:36.810
It's a cell phone.

51:36.810 --> 51:40.440
That's a phone?! You can carry it around?

51:40.440 --> 51:42.440
I knew it!

51:42.980 --> 51:46.560
So, can we make contact with the outside world?

51:46.560 --> 51:49.850
Can't! It's soaked.

51:49.850 --> 51:51.100
Probably a goner.

51:52.850 --> 51:57.150
So, um, do robots exist now?

51:57.600 --> 52:02.560
I saw a robot aisle at the hardware store the other day!

52:03.060 --> 52:04.150
Yeah?

52:04.150 --> 52:08.480
Yes! I knew it!

52:11.310 --> 52:13.400
How about flying cars?

52:13.690 --> 52:14.690
Huh?

52:16.690 --> 52:18.900
How long have you been here, exactly?

52:22.980 --> 52:26.400
More than thirty years.

52:28.770 --> 52:31.400
I had a big deal going down.

52:31.400 --> 52:34.850
I hid the goods in a manga case.

52:39.100 --> 52:40.940
But I took the wrong one.

52:46.150 --> 52:50.150
The coast guard and the feds knew all about it anyway.

52:52.980 --> 52:56.730
I was making a run for it, lights flashing everywhere...

52:57.560 --> 53:02.770
When a huge whale swallowed me!

53:03.230 --> 53:04.770
Couldn't believe it.

53:09.350 --> 53:10.690
And then what?

53:10.690 --> 53:13.940
I got caught in the waves,

53:14.810 --> 53:17.690
and when I came around it was pitch black.

53:18.520 --> 53:22.440
I tried to escape, but the waves were too rough.

53:22.810 --> 53:25.440
I tried over and over.

53:27.310 --> 53:32.520
I couldn't have survived without my friend.

53:35.560 --> 53:37.600
Um, where's the toilet?

53:37.600 --> 53:40.810
The washroom? Straight ahead!

53:40.810 --> 53:42.060
I'll take you!

53:42.060 --> 53:43.600
Nah, it's okay!

53:44.100 --> 53:45.730
Just straight ahead, right?

53:53.270 --> 53:54.100
No way!

54:09.980 --> 54:11.850
Hey, keep talking!

54:16.400 --> 54:17.350
Where's the back door?

54:17.350 --> 54:19.850
All the way down there!

54:19.850 --> 54:21.350
Oh, right!

54:21.350 --> 54:22.850
But of course!

54:23.350 --> 54:24.850
Back to square one!

54:25.270 --> 54:29.150
Got to know your own limits!

54:48.230 --> 54:50.020
We're outta here.

54:52.730 --> 54:53.980
We can go this way.

54:55.650 --> 54:58.020
It's wobbling.

54:58.520 --> 55:00.520
It's the only way. C'mon!

55:03.480 --> 55:04.810
It'll be all right!

55:08.940 --> 55:11.440
Don't go out there!

55:12.020 --> 55:14.230
It's meal time again!

55:14.650 --> 55:15.730
Hurry!

55:15.730 --> 55:17.730
Come back!

55:17.730 --> 55:19.060
Wait!

55:19.060 --> 55:20.560
The water's coming!

55:20.560 --> 55:21.770
Nishi!

55:25.520 --> 55:27.270
There! The exit!

55:29.060 --> 55:31.270
Put these on!

55:37.350 --> 55:39.190
Nishi! Come back!

55:40.770 --> 55:42.900
Nishi!

56:12.400 --> 56:14.100
Hey, let go of me!

56:31.900 --> 56:32.690
Nishi!

56:33.100 --> 56:34.560
You're awake!

56:34.940 --> 56:38.900
What a relief! He's come around!

56:40.230 --> 56:42.600
And here's something to cheer you up.

56:42.600 --> 56:46.560
<i>And a "Happy Mornin'" to y'all!</i>

56:46.560 --> 56:48.600
<i>Wow, is this a beautiful day or what?</i>

56:48.600 --> 56:55.400
<i>You wouldn't believe how blue the sky was this morning.</i>

56:55.400 --> 56:56.310
<i>Thing of real beauty!</i>

56:56.310 --> 57:00.940
<i>Yeah, I thought I'd drive all the way to Brazil, y'know?</i>

57:00.940 --> 57:04.310
<i>Well, it's gonna be booming at the resorts today!</i>

57:04.310 --> 57:07.850
<i>Certainly not a day for school or work, I tell ya!</i>

57:13.560 --> 57:16.650
Just wait a minute, I know it's scary.

57:16.650 --> 57:18.730
Well, this isn't what I expected.

57:18.730 --> 57:21.560
C'mon, cheer up!

57:21.560 --> 57:24.400
You're homesick. I've been there.

57:24.400 --> 57:27.480
I cried and got angry too.

57:27.480 --> 57:30.440
But I realized after coming here...

57:30.440 --> 57:33.400
Oh, whatever!

57:33.400 --> 57:36.690
I've got an idea! There's a place that'll cheer you up.

57:36.690 --> 57:38.480
My wonderful friend is there too!

57:38.480 --> 57:40.940
Let's go! Everybody!

57:42.940 --> 57:44.690
<i>Wrecked cars are popping up everywhere.</i>

57:44.690 --> 57:46.940
<i>Must've been some monster car chase.</i>

57:48.230 --> 57:51.400
You haven't eaten properly in 3 days!

57:51.400 --> 57:53.480
You're not gonna last that way!

57:53.480 --> 57:56.520
You need to eat for your breasts' sake!

57:56.520 --> 57:59.600
And Nishi, you've eaten nothing!

57:59.600 --> 58:01.440
Forget about getting it up!

58:03.440 --> 58:04.400
Hey!

58:05.690 --> 58:07.150
Just shut up, okay?

58:24.770 --> 58:26.100
Gramps,

58:26.100 --> 58:29.230
will you take me to that fun place you mentioned?

58:29.770 --> 58:32.520
Wanna go? It'll be great!

58:32.520 --> 58:33.600
I need a change.

58:33.600 --> 58:35.560
That's the spirit!

58:35.560 --> 58:37.480
You'll love it!

58:38.560 --> 58:39.730
Nishi?

58:39.730 --> 58:41.100
You too!

58:42.270 --> 58:44.850
Nah. Count me out.

58:44.850 --> 58:48.060
It'll be fun! You can meet my friend, too!

58:48.060 --> 58:50.650
Hearts'll sore! Heads'll explode!

58:50.650 --> 58:54.310
Cut it, gramps! I'm not in the mood!

58:54.310 --> 58:55.980
Just leave me alone!

58:58.480 --> 59:01.350
Join us later if you feel like it, okay?

59:01.350 --> 59:03.230
Let's go, Myon.

59:03.230 --> 59:05.690
Let's go, let's go!

59:05.690 --> 59:07.150
This'll be a blast!

59:07.650 --> 59:10.560
You'll love my friend.

59:23.230 --> 59:26.520
Fuck! The look on his face!

59:26.520 --> 59:28.730
He doesn't have a clue.

59:28.730 --> 59:32.900
I only said those things 'cause he was being inconsiderate!

59:32.900 --> 59:34.690
How about a little kindness, huh?

59:34.690 --> 59:36.560
I'm hurt!

59:38.650 --> 59:40.480
I have doubts about his humanity!

59:41.600 --> 59:45.310
What about my manga career?!

59:45.310 --> 59:47.020
What about my glorious campus life, huh?!

59:53.810 --> 59:54.310
Asshole!

59:54.310 --> 59:55.770
Loser!

01:00:23.100 --> 01:00:26.230
<i>30 years. 30 years.</i>

01:01:42.100 --> 01:01:44.310
<i>Gotta drink your milk, honey!</i>

01:01:59.980 --> 01:02:00.980
<i>30 years.</i>

01:02:29.100 --> 01:02:30.100
You okay?

01:02:30.100 --> 01:02:32.850
Isn't it amazing, Nishi? Were you surprised?

01:02:35.810 --> 01:02:39.310
Gramps, I...

01:02:39.310 --> 01:02:44.690
Er, I kind of just, back there...

01:02:48.270 --> 01:02:51.650
I'd become a bad person.

01:02:51.650 --> 01:02:54.650
I wanted to boast about my evil ways.

01:02:54.650 --> 01:02:58.400
I wanted to be known as a tough, rugged man!

01:02:58.400 --> 01:03:01.730
I wanted to walk over everybody.

01:03:03.350 --> 01:03:05.230
But I wound up here, and...

01:03:05.690 --> 01:03:07.730
I struggled.

01:03:07.730 --> 01:03:10.690
But I managed to survive!

01:03:11.560 --> 01:03:13.690
I can still swim!

01:03:13.690 --> 01:03:18.150
Still take things in my hands, still walk, still see!

01:03:18.940 --> 01:03:20.730
Isn't that fun?

01:03:20.730 --> 01:03:23.230
Seawater's salty!

01:03:23.230 --> 01:03:24.980
This place stinks!

01:03:24.980 --> 01:03:26.980
But it gives me joy!

01:03:26.980 --> 01:03:29.440
Would you rather lie around doing nothing?

01:03:29.440 --> 01:03:32.150
Or would you rather feel something?

01:03:32.730 --> 01:03:35.230
Which is more fun?

01:06:03.270 --> 01:06:04.850
She sure can swim.

01:06:04.850 --> 01:06:08.730
She was seriously trying to go to the Olympics till she was about 15.

01:06:08.730 --> 01:06:10.150
Had a coach and all.

01:06:10.150 --> 01:06:13.440
Come to think of it, I remember her winning something back in elementary school.

01:06:13.440 --> 01:06:15.310
Bronze at the Kinki Races.

01:06:16.230 --> 01:06:18.940
She stopped when her boobs got bigger in middle school.

01:06:18.940 --> 01:06:21.940
No kidding! For better or for worse, that.

01:06:21.940 --> 01:06:24.480
Yeah, for better or for worse!

01:06:26.980 --> 01:06:28.480
How is it?

01:06:31.440 --> 01:06:34.230
Wow! Fantastic!

01:06:34.230 --> 01:06:37.480
Right, my turn! Quality entertainment coming up!

01:06:56.230 --> 01:06:58.350
Got one!

01:06:58.350 --> 01:06:59.690
Nishi!

01:08:37.400 --> 01:08:40.810
Nishi, remember when we found a stray dog?

01:08:41.400 --> 01:08:42.730
In kindergarten?

01:08:43.480 --> 01:08:46.270
And you said you'd take care of it?

01:08:46.770 --> 01:08:49.270
That made me so happy!

01:08:49.270 --> 01:08:50.730
Yeah?

01:08:51.270 --> 01:08:54.810
I'm gonna take him home with me.

01:08:54.810 --> 01:08:57.480
You will? Thank you!

01:08:57.480 --> 01:09:00.900
I already have a sea-monkey, so it'll be fine!

01:09:02.350 --> 01:09:04.650
Wanna see?

01:09:04.650 --> 01:09:06.520
C'mon, I'll show ya.

01:09:07.150 --> 01:09:08.100
Myon.

01:09:09.350 --> 01:09:11.850
I was writing something.

01:09:12.230 --> 01:09:14.230
Far, far in the future,

01:09:14.230 --> 01:09:18.480
when the world is starving from overpopulation and environmental destruction,

01:09:19.480 --> 01:09:23.440
Earth decides to send a spaceship in search of food.

01:09:27.480 --> 01:09:29.190
But they get stranded.

01:09:32.060 --> 01:09:34.150
They land on a strange planet.

01:09:34.150 --> 01:09:38.850
There's water and oxygen, but nothing edible for humans.

01:09:42.400 --> 01:09:44.730
Except for one thing, they soon discover:

01:09:50.310 --> 01:09:53.440
A certain creature's poo.

01:09:54.600 --> 01:09:55.980
Pretty gross!

01:09:57.270 --> 01:10:00.690
And it's the perfect food for humans.

01:10:02.730 --> 01:10:06.600
But the creature's unbelievably bad at hunting and on the verge of extinction!

01:10:06.600 --> 01:10:08.100
There's only one?

01:10:09.520 --> 01:10:13.690
Our men help the creature hunt and look after it.

01:10:13.690 --> 01:10:16.020
And they live like that for a while,

01:10:16.020 --> 01:10:18.600
until a new enemy arrives.

01:10:19.270 --> 01:10:24.270
An evolved species of plant starts stealing the poop from them!

01:10:24.270 --> 01:10:26.600
A poo war, huh?

01:10:26.600 --> 01:10:29.650
But what happens to the crew then?

01:10:31.730 --> 01:10:35.270
Guess we need to send them home safely, huh?

01:10:35.270 --> 01:10:39.600
The planet is ideal in some ways, but...

01:10:40.270 --> 01:10:44.600
In fact, the planet's some kind of cell.

01:10:44.600 --> 01:10:48.230
Our crew must've ended up there after being shrunk!

01:10:48.230 --> 01:10:49.560
A cell?

01:10:49.560 --> 01:10:51.850
Yeah, of a human body.

01:10:51.850 --> 01:10:53.100
Whose?

01:10:53.400 --> 01:10:54.150
Yours!

01:10:54.150 --> 01:10:55.730
Mine?

01:10:55.730 --> 01:10:57.690
Let's just say.

01:10:58.270 --> 01:11:00.100
It was the leader's feelings.

01:11:00.690 --> 01:11:06.400
His love for his girl and his regret at not being able to complete his mission

01:11:06.400 --> 01:11:09.650
sent them there when they were on the brink of certain death.

01:11:10.440 --> 01:11:11.850
But one day,

01:11:11.850 --> 01:11:15.150
they realize their bodies have grown bigger.

01:11:15.150 --> 01:11:16.560
Why?

01:11:16.560 --> 01:11:17.810
Good question.

01:11:19.480 --> 01:11:21.230
And one day you hear a voice!

01:11:21.230 --> 01:11:23.980
From inside your tummy as you're sitting on the toilet.

01:11:23.980 --> 01:11:27.480
"Oh my God! We're growing bigger and bigger!"

01:11:27.480 --> 01:11:29.350
Well, that doesn't sound pleasant!

01:11:29.350 --> 01:11:31.020
But you can communicate that way.

01:11:31.020 --> 01:11:34.060
And they realize they're inside your stomach.

01:11:34.060 --> 01:11:34.810
Then what?

01:11:34.810 --> 01:11:35.480
They get out!

01:11:35.480 --> 01:11:35.980
From where?

01:11:35.980 --> 01:11:38.310
At this point, they're moving along the colon with the poop!

01:11:38.310 --> 01:11:39.480
Not happening!

01:11:39.810 --> 01:11:41.400
But what else can they do?

01:11:41.400 --> 01:11:43.400
They keep getting bigger.

01:11:43.400 --> 01:11:44.480
Your belly'll explode!

01:11:44.480 --> 01:11:45.230
I said no!

01:11:45.230 --> 01:11:47.480
"We're almost out, don't flush us!"

01:11:47.480 --> 01:11:49.480
I <i>am</i> flushing them!

01:11:49.480 --> 01:11:50.810
"We're out! We're out!"

01:11:52.400 --> 01:11:53.900
Nooo!

01:13:40.560 --> 01:13:42.400
Myon!

01:13:42.400 --> 01:13:44.100
Nishi!

01:13:44.100 --> 01:13:47.900
Nishi! Myon!

01:13:48.400 --> 01:13:49.770
We're up here!

01:13:49.770 --> 01:13:51.520
You guys okay?

01:13:51.520 --> 01:13:53.100
A-OK!

01:13:53.650 --> 01:13:58.230
I'm relieved! We were worried.

01:13:58.230 --> 01:14:01.600
Scared the hell out of me!
That was a total surprise!

01:14:19.650 --> 01:14:24.270
Told ya so! It's wicked, man! A miracle, I say!

01:14:24.270 --> 01:14:27.730
<i>The Other World</i> by Robin Nishi. The guy's a total genius!

01:14:28.480 --> 01:14:31.520
Cut class and meet me at the arcade!

01:14:31.520 --> 01:14:33.100
The Strawberry Plaza in ten!

01:14:33.100 --> 01:14:33.850
Roger that.

01:14:34.900 --> 01:14:37.190
This place is so, like, <i>capitalist</i>.

01:14:38.310 --> 01:14:39.900
Are you trying to be cool?

01:14:45.100 --> 01:14:45.730
Isn't that...

01:14:46.560 --> 01:14:49.560
Robin Nishi!

01:14:50.020 --> 01:14:51.480
I didn't even notice that.

01:14:52.560 --> 01:14:54.850
Check out the chicks!

01:14:54.850 --> 01:14:57.060
Awesome!

01:14:57.060 --> 01:15:00.480
Excuse me, you're Robin Nishi, right?

01:15:00.480 --> 01:15:02.060
Hiroshi, you idiot!

01:15:04.560 --> 01:15:05.560
Hell yeah, I am!

01:15:18.060 --> 01:15:19.480
Sorry!

01:15:19.480 --> 01:15:20.770
We're huge fans!

01:15:20.770 --> 01:15:23.480
<i>The Other World</i> rocks!

01:15:26.440 --> 01:15:28.350
Wanna grab a bite?

01:15:28.690 --> 01:15:29.650
Follow me!

01:15:29.650 --> 01:15:31.310
Seriously?!

01:15:34.190 --> 01:15:34.940
Eat!

01:15:34.940 --> 01:15:36.980
Thank you for the food!

01:15:37.940 --> 01:15:39.850
This is like your average day?

01:15:39.850 --> 01:15:40.480
Yeah!

01:15:40.480 --> 01:15:42.100
Awesome!

01:15:42.100 --> 01:15:43.810
I feel so alive!

01:15:43.810 --> 01:15:46.350
Robin, I'll pick up the tab!

01:15:46.350 --> 01:15:48.020
What are you talking about?

01:15:48.020 --> 01:15:49.310
Hiroshi, you idiot!

01:15:54.770 --> 01:15:58.730
Hiroshi, kids shouldn't worry about things like that.

01:15:58.730 --> 01:16:00.770
Have fun and grow up big!

01:16:01.600 --> 01:16:05.150
Not as a replica, but as someone who rises above!

01:16:12.100 --> 01:16:15.150
<i>We're here to witness the first contact with aliens!</i>

01:16:15.150 --> 01:16:20.770
<i>And directing this epic moment is the artist who made it all possible!</i>

01:16:20.770 --> 01:16:24.400
<i>Salvatore Antonio Yang Gogh!</i>

01:16:44.400 --> 01:16:47.400
<i>The cheers are rising here at the 1st Cosmic Swimming Contest.</i>

01:16:47.400 --> 01:16:53.060
<i>Representing Earth! Matt Beyond Thorpe Myon!</i>

01:16:55.350 --> 01:16:59.770
<i>And so the race begins as we witness history in the making!</i>

01:17:02.690 --> 01:17:05.060
<i>First corner and into the gate!</i>

01:17:05.060 --> 01:17:07.060
<i>Cameras are not allowed inside!</i>

01:17:15.100 --> 01:17:18.190
<i>And they're coming out! Four in the first group! And she's there!</i>

01:17:18.190 --> 01:17:21.810
<i>Matt Beyond Thorpe Myon, representing Earth!</i>

01:17:25.060 --> 01:17:26.810
Isn't this supposed to be extinct?

01:17:31.560 --> 01:17:32.560
This one, too!

01:19:30.600 --> 01:19:31.520
Think we can escape?

01:19:31.520 --> 01:19:32.690
Want to?

01:19:33.060 --> 01:19:35.810
We might be happier here.

01:19:53.980 --> 01:19:55.100
Jump!

01:20:16.810 --> 01:20:20.770
It shouldn't be time yet, and the water hadn't even receded that much.

01:20:23.690 --> 01:20:27.560
Thank goodness! I was about to go fetch you.

01:20:31.560 --> 01:20:32.900
Gramps.

01:20:32.900 --> 01:20:34.560
What's going on?

01:20:40.020 --> 01:20:42.980
The water level's increasing.

01:20:43.980 --> 01:20:47.060
And he's eating less.

01:20:47.480 --> 01:20:49.060
Meaning?

01:20:51.230 --> 01:20:53.350
Can't say for sure,

01:20:53.350 --> 01:20:55.060
but he could be dying.

01:20:55.810 --> 01:20:57.560
Dying?

01:20:57.560 --> 01:21:00.060
But what happens to us, then?

01:21:00.520 --> 01:21:02.350
Eventually, this place'll sink.

01:21:06.150 --> 01:21:09.190
We've gotta leave. It's that or drown.

01:21:09.190 --> 01:21:10.850
But how?

01:21:10.850 --> 01:21:12.730
By boat, of course!

01:21:12.730 --> 01:21:15.270
The cops'll be looking for us.

01:21:15.270 --> 01:21:15.690
So?

01:21:15.690 --> 01:21:18.230
The Yakuza'll come after us!

01:21:18.230 --> 01:21:19.350
So what!

01:21:19.350 --> 01:21:20.850
I wanna get out!

01:21:21.600 --> 01:21:23.520
'Cause there's so much out there!

01:21:23.520 --> 01:21:26.850
So many different people, living different lives!

01:21:26.850 --> 01:21:29.520
Incredibly good guys, bad guys!

01:21:29.520 --> 01:21:33.850
Folks completely different from us!
It's one huge melting pot!

01:21:33.850 --> 01:21:38.480
See, it's not about success, dying in the streets, who's better, who's not!

01:21:38.480 --> 01:21:39.980
I just want to be a part of it!

01:21:40.940 --> 01:21:44.600
I realized that even if I've got no connections,
no money, and no talent,

01:21:44.600 --> 01:21:46.600
even if I'm one big loser,

01:21:46.600 --> 01:21:51.270
I want to use my hands and feet to think and move, to shape my own life!

01:21:51.980 --> 01:21:53.900
We can just die here,

01:21:53.900 --> 01:21:56.150
or we can try!

01:21:56.150 --> 01:21:58.850
Let's see what we've got!

01:22:01.730 --> 01:22:03.480
It's impossible, though.

01:22:03.480 --> 01:22:05.850
Motivation's not gonna get us over that wave.

01:22:06.560 --> 01:22:08.230
We need a motorboat.

01:22:11.690 --> 01:22:13.520
We've got a motor!

01:22:13.520 --> 01:22:14.270
Right here!

01:22:17.810 --> 01:22:19.020
But there's no fuel.

01:22:20.270 --> 01:22:24.400
Sure there is! We came here by car, remember?

01:22:29.900 --> 01:22:30.650
Yes!

01:22:30.650 --> 01:22:31.560
It could work!

01:22:31.560 --> 01:22:32.900
It will work!

01:22:37.060 --> 01:22:39.230
We're going to make it!

01:22:39.980 --> 01:22:41.900
We're so gonna make it!

01:22:42.940 --> 01:22:43.980
Get up there!

01:23:43.650 --> 01:23:50.400
<i>The World Cup ends tomorrow with its final match.
The world waits for the winner to be crowned!</i>

01:23:50.730 --> 01:23:52.770
We're near Osaka again!

01:23:52.770 --> 01:23:53.600
Oh, yeah!

01:23:53.600 --> 01:23:57.190
I think this is our only chance.

01:23:57.190 --> 01:24:01.940
Maybe the whale's come here for our sake.

01:24:02.270 --> 01:24:03.940
We're going for it!

01:24:24.440 --> 01:24:25.190
...home with me.

01:24:35.690 --> 01:24:39.060
You're older. Lend it to her!

01:24:39.060 --> 01:24:40.480
I don't want to!

01:24:40.480 --> 01:24:41.480
Yang.

01:24:41.480 --> 01:24:44.440
Don't run like that, Myon'll follow you.

01:24:44.440 --> 01:24:46.190
Sorry, Myon.

01:24:48.310 --> 01:24:50.310
I don't like that uniform!

01:24:50.690 --> 01:24:51.400
I'll work.

01:24:51.400 --> 01:24:52.810
Sorry, Yang.

01:25:00.020 --> 01:25:00.900
Wanna try?

01:25:08.980 --> 01:25:09.940
Myon.

01:25:19.400 --> 01:25:20.480
Yang!

01:25:21.350 --> 01:25:22.810
Thanks!

01:25:24.100 --> 01:25:27.150
I'm not gonna let you carry all the load anymore.

01:25:27.150 --> 01:25:28.940
I'll grow up.

01:25:30.270 --> 01:25:31.770
I'm sorry.

01:25:31.770 --> 01:25:35.600
I always knew you were the one that needed support.

01:25:38.980 --> 01:25:43.060
It's your turn now.

01:25:43.060 --> 01:25:44.520
Go ahead!

01:26:12.650 --> 01:26:15.520
Here we go, kids!

01:26:17.020 --> 01:26:20.350
Yes, sir!

01:28:04.230 --> 01:28:10.100
Water striders float using surface tension from the hairs on the bottom of their legs.

01:28:33.230 --> 01:28:33.730
I'm sorry.

01:29:03.150 --> 01:29:06.310
Your bones won't get strong if you don't drink milk.

01:29:06.310 --> 01:29:07.440
Yes, mom!

01:29:13.270 --> 01:29:16.020
Oh, not again.

01:29:16.690 --> 01:29:18.770
I'll have to cook it in, then.

01:33:12.650 --> 01:33:14.980
This'll be perfect right here.

01:33:16.230 --> 01:33:17.480
Wrong, idiot!

01:33:17.480 --> 01:33:18.940
The baby!

01:33:19.600 --> 01:33:20.650
You okay?

01:33:20.650 --> 01:33:22.730
It's heavy!

01:33:22.730 --> 01:33:23.850
There!

01:33:24.600 --> 01:33:27.940
Too much space for a little kid, don't you think?

01:33:27.940 --> 01:33:30.060
He'll be big in no time.

01:33:30.060 --> 01:33:31.600
Wonder what he'll be like.

01:33:35.350 --> 01:33:38.980
Be right there, sweetie!

01:33:39.770 --> 01:33:43.730
Your fever's just gone down, you know.

01:33:43.730 --> 01:33:44.600
I'm fine.

01:33:44.600 --> 01:33:46.350
See you later.

01:33:47.150 --> 01:33:48.270
See you at 10!

01:33:48.850 --> 01:33:50.600
Keiko? It's me!

01:33:51.190 --> 01:33:52.560
Myon?

01:33:52.560 --> 01:33:54.020
I've got an art show.

01:33:54.020 --> 01:33:55.520
That's great!

01:33:55.850 --> 01:33:57.520
<i>And she's going for the rope!</i>

01:33:58.520 --> 01:34:00.520
We've got no money either!

01:34:01.520 --> 01:34:02.270
<i>Worn by!</i>

01:34:05.600 --> 01:34:06.690
There, found it!

01:34:06.980 --> 01:34:07.440
Jun!

01:34:07.980 --> 01:34:08.940
Wait long?

01:34:09.940 --> 01:34:11.940
That's insane! They're Yakuzas!

01:34:12.230 --> 01:34:16.690
I told you to wait till tomorrow, so shut up and wait, you punk!

01:34:17.940 --> 01:34:21.400
Sorry about that! Now back to your interview!

01:34:57.690 --> 01:34:58.520
That's her!

01:35:24.310 --> 01:35:25.480
Myon!

01:40:49.230 --> 01:41:00.350
I remember when I put a short, sweet, and unpracticed kiss on your cheek

01:41:00.350 --> 01:41:09.850
On the day when if our eyes met while we messed around we'd quickly look away

01:41:09.850 --> 01:41:18.230
As we were lit by the gently flickering morning light

01:41:19.980 --> 01:41:27.650
My sadness, my sins, my hypocrisy, my mistakes

01:41:27.650 --> 01:41:32.060
If I'm with you, I can overcome them all

01:41:33.650 --> 01:41:38.560
I had always believed that

01:41:38.560 --> 01:41:48.100
Please don't forget the sound of my voice calling you

01:41:48.100 --> 01:41:57.850
Don't ever tell anyone else those secrets we shared

01:41:57.850 --> 01:42:08.020
Your all-too-slimmed shoulders were so so dear to me

01:42:08.020 --> 01:42:12.150
Even should we never meet again

01:42:12.150 --> 01:42:17.100
You were my first and last love
